name 'pl-aif-y2-u1-l3-hello-ai-facilitation'
title 'title'
description 'description here'

markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Facilitating First Syntax Errors

Students are building their first real Python programs here, which means they're hitting their first real syntax errors too. The deck is explicit about this moment: remind students that mistakes and debugging are a normal part of programming, not a sign something's gone wrong with them.

## What's Actually Happening in This Lesson

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
    <div style="background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12px; width: 24px; height: 24px; min-width: 24px; border-radius: 6px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">1</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><strong>Build a Chatbot (Levels 1-3):</strong> students print a greeting, then use a variable to personalize it, then use variables of different data types to print today's date</div>
  </div>
  <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px;">
    <div style="background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 12px; width: 24px; height: 24px; min-width: 24px; border-radius: 6px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">2</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><strong>Asking Questions (Levels 4-6):</strong> students extend the chatbot to accept user input, introducing concepts beyond what this PL module covers in depth</div>
  </div>
</div>

<hr>

## Watch for: Missing Quotation Marks

<div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; margin: 20px 0; flex-wrap: wrap;">
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 250px; background-color: #FFE3CE; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #611D00; margin-bottom: 10px;">Stuck: Missing Quotes</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #611D00; line-height: 1.6; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Courier New', monospace;">print(Hello!)</div>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 250px; background-color: #CCF1D0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #003F25; margin-bottom: 10px;">Strong: Quoted as Text</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #003F25; line-height: 1.6; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Courier New', monospace;">print("Hello!")</div>
  </div>
</div>

### Watch for: F-String Syntax

<div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; margin: 20px 0; flex-wrap: wrap;">
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 250px; background-color: #FFE3CE; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #611D00; margin-bottom: 10px;">Stuck: Missing f or Braces</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #611D00; line-height: 1.6; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Courier New', monospace;">print("Hi, name!")</div>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 250px; background-color: #CCF1D0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
    <div style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #003F25; margin-bottom: 10px;">Strong: f Prefix and Braces</div>
    <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #003F25; line-height: 1.6; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Courier New', monospace;">print(f"Hi, {name}!")</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;">
    <strong>&#128161; Language to borrow:</strong>
  </div>
  <div style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: bold; color: #4C42CF; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-top: 16px; margin-bottom: 8px;">For missing quotation marks</div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222;">&bull; "Python uses quotation marks to tell apart code from text. What happens if you add them back?"</div>

  <div style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: bold; color: #4C42CF; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-top: 16px; margin-bottom: 8px;">For f-string mistakes</div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222;">&bull; "Does this string start with an f? Is the variable name inside curly braces?"</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #D5EFFF; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; margin-top: 20px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #06338D; line-height: 1.6;">
    <strong>&#8505; Note:</strong> Levels 4-6 introduce input() and converting text to numbers, concepts this PL module doesn't cover in depth. If students hit errors there, the same debugging mindset applies: mistakes are normal, and reading the error message is the first step, not a dead end.
  </div>
</div>
MARKDOWN
